// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_band_orphan_restore.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: OWN-2's ON-op count — a restore whose id names no ON op
//          (band-ownership design §3.2, the "restore with no ON op" row of §3.3).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "has 0 ON op(s) carrying its id"
//
// A restore built DIRECTLY as the enum variant, carrying a plausible band id (the one
// `band(100, ..., stream_cram($48, ...))` would derive, 100 * 128 + $48) and no ON op
// anywhere. It streams this frame's BASE palette over CRAM entry 36 at line 140, undoing
// something nothing ever did.
//
// WHY THE HAND-BUILT VARIANT, and it is the same argument the $8F/$8A scans rest on:
// `RasterOp` is `pub` (its arms are the wire contract), so `RasterOp.PalRestore(a, n, id)`
// is a spelling the language admits and `band()` cannot see. Constructor-only refusals are
// not refusals. This is the layer that cannot be dodged.
//
// C-A REFUSED THIS TOO, by a different route — its `isect_earlier == 0` count — and that
// row of the design's succession table is what this poison holds. The difference is that
// C-A's version of the sentence described the guard ("0 strictly-earlier ops intersect the
// restore's span") where this one describes the program.
//
// ONE WORD, not three, and the count below is why: the walk carries one `poisoned` flag
// PER CRAM ENTRY, so a three-word orphan would say the same true thing three times over.
// A one-entry span makes the fixture report exactly one sentence per guard.
//
// COUNT 2: OWN-2's ON-op count, plus OWN-1 seeing the same fact from the other side — a
// restore closing band 12872 on an entry where no band is live. Both are real and neither
// is a cascade of the other; they are the pairing layer and the timeline layer agreeing.
//
// NO IMPORTS — see poison_four_bands.emp's note.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_band_orphan_restore

const POISON_BAND_ORPHAN_RESTORE = [
    fire(140, [RasterOp.PalRestore($48, 1, 100 * 128 + $48)]),
]

ensure(raster_program(POISON_BAND_ORPHAN_RESTORE).len > 0,
       "poison_band_orphan_restore: raster_program returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
